flowchart TB
  accTitle: A min-heap is not a binary search tree
  accDescr: Array [1,2,9,5] represents a min-heap: index zero has value one and children at indexes one and two with values two and nine. Index one has a left child at index three with value five. Parent values never exceed their children, but left children need not be smaller than parents.
  A["index 0: value 1"] -->|Left child| B["index 1: value 2"]
  A -->|Right child| C["index 2: value 9"]
  B -->|Left child| D["index 3: value 5"]

